# SessionsList / SessionRow — every device signed in as you, and a way to
# throw one out. `profile/AccountSecurity`'s own note says plainly what is
# NOT its job ("No crypto and no session/device management live here") — this
# is that other half, in the category that owns identity rather than the one
# that owns the profile.
#
#     use SettingsSection("Sessions", ""):
#         use SessionsList():
#             for s in Session where s.user == actor by lastActive desc limit 50:
#                 use SessionRow(s)
#
# ── `SessionRow` TAKES THE ROW, THE WAY `graph/FriendRequestRow` DOES ────────
#
# `Session` is not declared here — the same reason `FriendRequestRow(r:
# FriendRequest)` names a type it never defines: the host's own `data` facet
# owns the entity (device, location, last-seen, which one this is), and this
# file only knows the five fields it renders. `revokeSession(id)` is a fixed
# action for the same reason `accept(id)`/`decline(id)` are on that file: a
# row already knows which session it is, so the call needs no reference
# threaded through a parameter, and the host's own `revokeSession` can
# `requires` the row belongs to the caller the way any action in this library
# guards a write.
#
# ── THE CURRENT SESSION HAS NO REVOKE BUTTON ─────────────────────────────────
#
# Ending the session you are reading this list FROM is `auth/SignOutButton`,
# not a row in it — a "Revoke" that logs the reader out from under themselves,
# sitting next to nine that do not, is the one button on this screen worth a
# different word and a different place entirely. `s.current` only ever
# renders the badge that says which row that is; it decides nothing else.
app FacetAuth:
    css:
        [data-fa-mount] .x-session { display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-items: center;
                     gap: 12px; padding: 12px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--x-line, #2f3336); }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-session-body { flex: 1; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-session-head { display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
    component SessionsList():
        box class "x-sessions":
            slot
    component SessionRow(s: Session):
        row class "x-session":
            box class "x-session-body":
                row class "x-session-head":
                    text "{s.device}" class "x-strong"
                    if s.current:
                        badge "This device" class "x-pill x-light"
                text "{s.location} · active {ago(s.lastActive)}" class "x-muted x-small"
            if !s.current:
                button "Revoke" -> revokeSession(s.id) class "x-pill"
